{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "6ffc1e3d-de2d-854d-9069-4dd068ef19bd",
  "created_at": "2026-03-10T15:15:31-04:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Public Works",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Paulo Souza",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Lorraine Medeiros",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T15:13:41-04:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Public Works, this is Lorraine. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T15:13:45-04:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hi, yeah, sorry, I'm whispering. Somebody's sleeping in the next room. I'm calling about the water again on my street."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T15:13:52-04:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No problem, take your time. Whereabouts is the water?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T15:13:56-04:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "285 Dixon Street, up the North End. Every time it rains hard, the water comes down the hill from the next street and goes straight into the yard. Straight in. After the rain Friday into Saturday, three days ago, it was standing out there till Monday."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T15:14:11-04:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "285 Dixon Street, and the water is coming down from the next street over into your yard. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T15:14:18-04:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Right. And nobody has done anything about it. It keeps happening. [pause] There's an older neighbor next door who can't get out when it's like that. She can't step through it, so she's stuck in the house."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T15:14:30-04:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Oh, that's not good. So she's stuck inside until it drains off."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T15:14:35-04:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah. So, is it a city drain or a state one? Nobody can tell me."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T15:14:40-04:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Well, it depends on the road. If it's a city street, the drain is ours. State roads are handled by the state. I'd have someone look at where it's coming from."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T15:14:50-04:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, so you send it to, what, Public Service? Is that a different office than you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T15:14:56-04:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Public Works, that's us. Same office you called. I'll put in a request for a crew to check the drains on Dixon and the street above it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T15:15:05-04:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. Good. Because I've said this before and it just sits there."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T15:15:09-04:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I understand. Let me read back what I have. 285 Dixon Street, North End, runoff coming down from the next street into the yard, after the weekend rain, and an elderly neighbor who can't get out. Is there a number to reach you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T15:15:23-04:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, 401-555-0160."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T15:15:25-04:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Got it, 401-555-0160. Someone will follow up."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T15:15:28-04:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. Thanks. I gotta go, she's waking up."
    }
  ],
